course: dictionary
lesson: 15436
title: Stature: height and importance
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Stature is a noun that can mean two things. The first is simple: how tall a person is when standing. «The little boy was of small stature, so he needed a box to see over the counter.» Here stature means height.
explain: The second meaning is more formal. It means the respect and importance someone has earned, often because of what they have done. «The scientist was a person of great stature, and everyone listened when she spoke.» Here stature means respect, not height.
explain: To choose the right meaning, read the clues around the word. If the sentence talks about a body, a size or how high someone reaches, stature means height. If it talks about fame, respect or what someone has achieved, stature means importance. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it.
fact: Stature is a noun.
fact: Stature usually has no plural, so we say «stature», not «statures».
fact: «Stature» means how tall a person is when standing.
fact: «Stature» can also mean respect and importance, often in formal writing, as in «a person of stature».
fact: Useful phrases: «of short stature», «of great stature», «grow in stature».
exercise: «The little girl was of small stature, so she could not reach the top shelf.» What does stature mean here? | *How tall she is | How fast she runs | How much money she has | How loudly she speaks
exercise: «The judge was a person of great stature, and everyone listened when she spoke.» What does stature mean here? | Speed | Height | The colour of her hair | *Respect and importance
exercise: «The man of short stature stood by the door.» Find and copy the word that tells you stature means height. | man | door | *short | stood
test: «The author was a writer of great stature, known around the world.» What does stature mean? | Money | Height | *Importance and respect | Speed
test: «The boy was of small stature and had to stand on a box to see.» What does stature mean? | Colour | Respect | *Height | Speed
exam: Which sentence uses stature to mean height? | *«The boy of short stature could not see over the crowd.» | «She is a person of stature in the community.» | «The scientist's stature grew with every discovery.» | «The mayor was a figure of great stature in the town.»
